      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm sorry to hear that you're experiencing a severe headache. While sumatriptan can be effective in reducing migraine symptoms, it's generally recommended to wait a bit before taking it to see if your medication isn't the cause of the migraine. Some people can be \"medication-overuse\" headache sufferers, which could lead to recent or worsening of symptoms. Try waiting 24-48 hours before taking sumatriptan again to avoid possible medication overuse.",
